{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1770 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ed774326424eae802a9d765d41ffe3f857edd46544992b57a355b87385f08219" :edb/db-before-t 1769 :edb/db-after-t 1770 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535082 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:25:25.879Z" 13194139535082 true] [17592186129198 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330228 13194139535082 true] [17592186129217 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330249 13194139535082 true] [17592186129218 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330235 13194139535082 true] [17592186129218 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330242 13194139535082 true] [17592186129462 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535082 true] [17592186129462 1100 "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1, 5)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $δA$. Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T$, given by\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln (uv) \\\\ uv^{2}\\end{bmatrix}$?" 13194139535082 false] [17592186129462 1100 "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,5)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv) \\\\ u{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139535082 true] [17592186129462 1145 "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v} \\\\ {v}^{2} & 2uv\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2uv-\\frac{1}{v}\\cdot {v}^{2} \\\\  & =2v-v \\\\  & =v \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,5)} & =v\\,{|}_{u=1\\,v=5} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|5|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =5\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330228 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330229 13194139535082 true] [17592186330228 1089 "q-160431" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330228 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535082 true] [17592186330228 1100 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2}+uv \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330228 1113 #uuid "8684eb9a-aecb-5b80-9a18-39831797ddaa" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330228 1145 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={v}^{2}+uv$ and $y(u,v)=v-u.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v+u \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 2v+u \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot 1-(2v+u)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =v+2v+u \\\\  & =3v+u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(8,-2)}=3(-2)+8=2.\n$$" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330230 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330231 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330232 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330233 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330234 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1041 "selection" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330231 13194139535082 true] [17592186330229 1110 #uuid "b4572c86-e93d-5e3c-a174-ade926d35fb8" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330230 1034 "3" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330230 1111 #uuid "5690df46-71a1-5cb9-a07f-efc829b9df70" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330231 1034 "2" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330231 1111 #uuid "c5edfcd2-dd83-5487-ade5-2dbfa1584ce7" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330232 1034 "6" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330232 1111 #uuid "f5a0d500-a743-5d8a-a25d-b2b64d7fd910" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330233 1034 "1" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330233 1111 #uuid "8c2c1b13-f9f5-5e24-9af5-2590bd3067f9" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330234 1034 "4" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330234 1111 #uuid "c2b96b26-5147-5789-aea3-83d401f9227e" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330235 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330236 13194139535082 true] [17592186330235 1089 "q-161841" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330235 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535082 true] [17592186330235 1100 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ -uv\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330235 1113 #uuid "a4aa2b6c-6ba5-59e1-9b2a-ad9aa14c6d6f" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330235 1145 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ -uv\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ -v & -u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot (-u)-(-v)\\cdot {e}^{u+v} \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}(v-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v}(v-u) & >0 \\\\ v-u & >0 \\\\ v & >u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(2,3)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png)" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330237 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330238 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330239 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330240 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330241 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1041 "selection" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330240 13194139535082 true] [17592186330236 1110 #uuid "2f2324bd-a56c-5887-a3ec-441980720cd6" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330237 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/fd2a51ca3a1654c2e857018268bf251366472a2c5d7f90009d5ccfbf1b1edd9d.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330237 1111 #uuid "53d1e293-06b2-518f-8f9b-a10697d6d1eb" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330238 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330238 1111 #uuid "9a7134ee-8c28-59d6-a54f-adfefbf5ecf3" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330239 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/0b764651dbc7999e7af13214685796b5045fab89f101bbc72bf413112df3c51f.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330239 1111 #uuid "ceff3973-b932-5863-9389-10a06bad9c8a" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330240 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330240 1111 #uuid "cb669985-40db-5692-a60c-c3b9cc709d9c" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330241 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330241 1111 #uuid "39a831ca-653e-550e-9ae8-ffc0bbd466f5" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330242 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330243 13194139535082 true] [17592186330242 1089 "q-161842" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330242 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535082 true] [17592186330242 1100 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330242 1113 #uuid "cbe9b704-1e10-5076-bbdf-dcc611074143" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330242 1145 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3{u}^{2} & -v \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3{u}^{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})-(1)\\cdot (-v) \\\\  & =v-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v-{u}^{2} & <0 \\\\ v & <{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv={u}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png)" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330244 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330245 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330246 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330247 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330248 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1041 "selection" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330248 13194139535082 true] [17592186330243 1110 #uuid "dfd9a1f1-a636-5ee9-ae67-ec4acbf86a5a" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330244 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330244 1111 #uuid "a126364a-f956-5e49-bd74-b5b7522d04e6" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330245 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/cb5b22ff46569b231d122c2ed11bd412907f36271a033d86769435adf9fe48c7.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330245 1111 #uuid "4b559133-9776-5227-9499-09dcc827c59c" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330246 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330246 1111 #uuid "ad35d12a-f398-5a5d-acc5-a836f5772e4d" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330247 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330247 1111 #uuid "6a5f5601-4637-55d5-b428-21d93926212c" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330248 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535082 true] [17592186330248 1111 #uuid "fcd52064-7688-5a56-95c8-dc10439372bc" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330249 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330250 13194139535082 true] [17592186330249 1089 "q-161875" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330249 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535082 true] [17592186330249 1100 "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(0,3)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u-{v}^{2} \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330249 1113 #uuid "48dd5630-af2d-5230-b0b6-01fe1c189191" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330249 1145 "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & -2v \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-2v) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+2v \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(0,3)} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+2v)\\,{|}_{u=0\\,v=3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2(3) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|6|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =6\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330251 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330252 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330253 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330254 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330255 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1041 "selection" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330254 13194139535082 true] [17592186330250 1110 #uuid "ff2be419-665e-5ed8-8086-6aa2b42cecac" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330251 1034 "12\\,\\delta A" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330251 1111 #uuid "b8cfebaf-5910-5742-8a6c-15a471b79c7b" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330252 1034 "16\\,\\delta A" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330252 1111 #uuid "abfd9700-88b9-5b3c-9dc3-ff3b93c6c55a" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330253 1034 "3\\,\\delta A" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330253 1111 #uuid "7616b827-891b-5b8a-9129-bc087ac3f20a" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330254 1034 "6\\,\\delta A" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330254 1111 #uuid "268f3950-be53-5ecc-9de8-6ef635325811" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330255 1034 "9\\,\\delta A" 13194139535082 true] [17592186330255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535082 true] [17592186330255 1111 #uuid "0d2aa81a-44a9-